<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Rothmans half year net profit jumps.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Rothmans half year net profit jumps.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>		  (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   86.23 vs   9.37</p>
<p>    Net				    52.06 vs   0.11</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		   25.0  vs  20.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Rothmans Holdings Ltd is a cigarette manufacturer and is about 50 percent owned by Rothmans International Ltd which in turn is 60 percent owned by Swiss-based Richemont AG and 40 percent by South African group Rembrandt Group Ltd  </p>
<p>    Sales			 865.83 vs  804.89</p>
<p>    Other income		 10.01 vs   10.39</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)		  42.7  vs   0.10</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		 nil vs loss 10.00</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date Nov 27</p>
<p>Reg date Nov 18</p>
<p>    Tax		  charge 32.82 vs credit 2.08</p>
<p>    Interest (thousands)     585  vs   148</p>
<p>    Depreciation		16.33 vs  16.49</p>
<p>    Minorities		   1.35 vs   1.34</p>
</text>
